   "source": [
    "## Visualising SMILES strings using RDKit\n",
    "\n",
    "RDKit is a very powerful package for all sorts of data science tasks in the life sciences. One function is to draw the structure for a SMILES code, by converting it into a Mol object."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 14,
   "id": "c6d94d55",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from rdkit import Chem\n",
    "from rdkit.Chem import Draw"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 16,
   "execution_count": 15,
   "id": "368d3ad0",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "smiles = \"C1CC2CCN1CC2\"\n",
    "\n",
    "mol_object = Chem.MolFromSmiles(smiles)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 17,
   "execution_count": 4,
   "id": "9944d55f",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
